r sources.\r\n\r\n### Basic mutual exclusion\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- coverage: R03-06 --\u003e\r\n\u003e [!todo] Seed\r\n\u003e To be written; see the coverage matrix row for sources.\r\n\r\n### Function call and return in the machine\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- coverage: R03-07 --\u003e\r\n\u003e [!todo] Seed\r\n\u003e To be written; see the coverage matrix row for sources.\r\n\r\n### Process memory layout\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- coverage: R03-08 --\u003e\r\n\u003e [!todo] Seed\r\n\u003e To be written; see the coverage matrix row for sources.\r\n\r\n### Pointers, function pointers, and casts\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- coverage: R03-09 --\u003e\r\n\u003e [!todo] Seed\r\n\u003e To be written; see the coverage matrix row for sources.\r\n\r\n### Compiling and linking\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- coverage: R03-10 --\u003e\r\n\u003e [!todo] Seed\r\n\u003e To be written; see the coverage matrix row for sources.\r\n\r\n### Segfaults and how to debug them\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- coverage: R03-11 --\u003e\r\n\u003e [!todo] Seed\r\n\u003e To be written; see the coverage matrix row for sources.\r\n\r\n### Pthreads producer-consumer\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- coverage: R03-12 --\u003e\r\n\u003e [!todo] Seed\r\n\u003e To be written; see the coverage matrix row for sources.\r\n\r\n## Mechanisms step by step\r\n\r\n\u003e [!todo] Seed\r\n\u003e To be written; see the coverage matrix row for sources.\r\n\r\n## Worked examples\r\n\r\n\u003e [!todo] Seed\r\n\u003e To be written; see the coverage matrix row for sources.\r\n\r\n## Comparison\r\n\r\n\u003e [!todo] Seed\r\n\u003e To be written; see the coverage matrix row for sources.\r\n\r\n## Paper deep dives\r\n\r\n- No paper for this lesson.\r\n\r\n## Modern descendants\r\n\r\n\u003e [!todo] Seed\r\n\u003e To be written; see the coverage matrix row for sources.\r\n\r\n## Pitfalls and exam traps\r\n\r\n\u003e [!todo] Seed\r\n\u003e To be written; see the coverage matrix row for sources.\r\n\r\n## Practice\r\n\r\n- [Practice R](../Practice/Practice-R.md)\r\n\r\n## Lab\r\n\r\n- [lab-00-refresher](../labs/lab-00-refresher/README.md): Refresher: page faults, TLB, caches, and a pthreads producer-consumer\r\n\r\n## Further reading\r\n\r\n\u003e [!todo] Seed\r\n\u003e To be written; see the coverage matrix row for sources.\r\n"}}}
